{title: The Turning Tide}
{artist: Campfire Tests}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The [C]tide went out at [G]morning and the [C]boats lay on the [G]sand
The [C]gulls were calling [G]over all the [C]flat and silver [G]land
We [C]counted every [G]mooring and we [C]counted every [G]rope
And [C]waited for the [G]water with our [C]pockets full of [G]hope
The [C]nets were hung for [G]mending and the [C]sails were folded [G]tight
The [C]harbour lamps were [G]burning though the [C]sky was full of [G]light
The [C]children ran the [G]shingle and the [C]old men watched the [G]bay
And [C]no one spoke of [G]sailing on that [C]long and quiet [G]day
{end_of_verse}

{key: D}
{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Then the [Bm]wind came round the [F#m]headland and the [Bm]water turned to [F#m]grey
And the [Bm]bell rang in the [F#m]chapel at the [Bm]closing of the [F#m]day
We [Bm]pulled the boats up [F#m]higher and we [Bm]tied the shutters [F#m]down
And the [Bm]sea came over [F#m]shingle to the [Bm]edges of the [F#m]town
It [Bm]roared along the [F#m]harbour and it [Bm]shook the wooden [F#m]pier
It [Bm]took the nets and [F#m]lanterns that we'd [Bm]hung there every [F#m]year
We [Bm]watched it from the [F#m]hillside till the [Bm]last of it was [F#m]gone
And the [Bm]morning found us [F#m]waiting for the [Bm]light to come up [F#m]on
The [Bm]sand was full of [F#m]timber and the [Bm]road was full of [F#m]stone
And [Bm]every house was [F#m]standing but the [Bm]harbour wall was [F#m]thrown
We [Bm]counted all the [F#m]neighbours and we [Bm]counted every [F#m]boat
And [Bm]not a soul was [F#m]missing and the [Bm]old ones kept a[F#m]float
The [Bm]priest said it was [F#m]mercy and the [Bm]fishers said it was [F#m]luck
And the [Bm]children found a [F#m]lobster in the [Bm]wreck of Martin's [F#m]truck
We [Bm]built the wall up [F#m]stronger through the [Bm]weeks of early [F#m]spring
And we [Bm]sang the old songs [F#m]louder than we'd [Bm]ever dared to [F#m]sing
{end_of_bridge}

{key: C}
{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The [Am]tide came in at [F]evening and the [Am]boats rose from the [F]sand
The [Am]gulls went still and [F]quiet over [Am]all the shining [F]land
We [Am]untied every [F]mooring and we [Am]coiled up every [F]rope
And [Am]rowed out on the [F]water with our [Am]pockets full of [F]hope
{end_of_verse}
